{
 "summary": "Updates the `generateblock` RPC to accept multiple coinbase outputs (addresses, descriptors, or objects specifying fixed satoshi amounts per recipient), distributing remaining block subsidy and fees evenly among them, or burning to an OP_RETURN output if omitted. It also makes the `transactions` parameter optional, falling back to mining from the mempool when omitted while preserving explicit empty or custom transaction lists.",
 "problem": "Developers and testers experimenting with mining pool payouts (such as Ocean or Braidpool) on regtest cannot create blocks with multiple coinbase outputs using `generateblock`, requiring manual block construction. Additionally, `generateblock` previously required an explicit transaction list and could not automatically mine transactions from the mempool.",
 "evidence": [
